# the parallel loops give the same answers at every width
# RUN: parallel-loops
# RUN: parallel-loops threads=2
# RUN: parallel-loops threads=16
# CHECK: each index once: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: nested loops: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: the longest indices first: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: collect: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: find: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: sort: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: sort and remove duplicates: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: tasks: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: width one is serial: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: worker numbers are below the width and unique at one time: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: build thread has the worker stack size: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: pool threads have the worker stack size: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: loops run on a host pool: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: one index asks for no helper: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: a helper that comes late does nothing: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: no more helpers than indices: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: a thread gets its storage back: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: an array creates and destroys each element once: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: resting threads take the next loop: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: short loops run in a scope: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: resting threads go back to the pool: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: ordered commit: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: pending tasks run by priority: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: a background loop yields to foreground loops: ok
# CHECK-NEXT: tasks run after their dependencies: ok
